Question 20: Install Terraform locally and write a configuration to provision an AWS EC2 instance. Extend the configuration to create a VPC and subnet, use variables and outputs, and verify the Terraform state using terraform plan, terraform apply and terraform destroy.
Commands & Steps:
mkdir terraform-q20-full-lab
cd terraform-q20-full-lab
nano main.tf
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply -auto-approve
terraform destroy


Configuration File (main.tf):
# Configure the AWS Provider
provider "aws" {
  region = "ap-south-1"
}

# 1. Create a VPC
resource "aws_vpc" "lab_vpc" {
  cidr_block           = "10.0.0.0/16"
  enable_dns_hostnames = true
  tags = {
    Name = "Lab-vpc"
  }
}

# 2. Create a Subnet inside the VPC
resource "aws_subnet" "lab_subnet" {
  vpc_id                  = aws_vpc.lab_vpc.id
  cidr_block              = "10.0.1.0/24"
  map_public_ip_on_launch = true
  tags = {
    Name = "Lab-subnet"
  }
}

# 3. Create an EC2 Instance inside the Subnet
resource "aws_instance" "lab_ec2" {
  ami           = "ami-019324397f534581" # Example AMI ID
  instance_type = "t3.micro"
  subnet_id     = aws_subnet.lab_subnet.id
  tags = {
    Name = "Lab-ec2-Instance"
  }
}



